Third-party notices for demos/read_aloud

This demo's source is part of XR Blocks (Apache License 2.0, see the LICENSE
file at the repository root). server/matcha_tts.py is adapted from the
"Text → Speech" web demo in google-ai-edge/litert-samples (samples/web_demos),
Apache License 2.0,
https://github.com/google-ai-edge/litert-samples/blob/main/LICENSE

Assets downloaded at runtime by the laptop server (nothing is redistributed in
this repository):

- Matcha-TTS LiteRT models and glue data (matcha_textenc_fp16.tflite,
  matcha_decoder_fp16.tflite, matcha_vocoder_fp16.tflite, emb.bin,
  config.json, g2p_meta.json)
  https://huggingface.co/litert-community/Matcha-TTS
  License: MIT. Converted from Matcha-TTS (MIT,
  https://github.com/shivammehta25/Matcha-TTS) and HiFi-GAN (MIT,
  https://github.com/jik876/hifi-gan).

- DeepPhonemizer G2P model (dp_g2p_matcha_fp16.tflite)
  https://github.com/as-ideas/DeepPhonemizer — License: MIT

- OpenPhonemizer espeak-IPA dictionary (g2p_dict.txt.gz)
  https://github.com/NeuralVox/OpenPhonemizer — License: Clear BSD

Python dependencies (installed by the user, not vendored):

- ai-edge-litert — Apache License 2.0
- numpy — BSD 3-Clause
